@page "/docs/troubleshooting/empty-selection"

@* An empty CheckboxGroup or MultiSelect posts nothing: the model isn't bound and the page's
   defaults come back, or the list is null when other fields post. Checked against Blazor's form
   binding (.NET 10) and in form-empty-selection in all three modes. *@

<ArticlePage Section="troubleshooting" Slug="empty-selection">
    <Lead>
        Set default choices only on the first load, not after a post, and read a missing list as empty.
    </Lead>
    <ChildContent>
        <Heading Level="2">Problem</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            On a static page, a reader unchecks every box in a <Code>CheckboxGroup</Code> and saves. The page comes back
            with the default boxes checked again, as if they'd never been unchecked. In a form with other fields, the list
            arrives as <Code>null</Code> instead, and code that reads <Code>.Count</Code> throws. A
            <Code>MultiSelect</Code> with nothing selected does the same.
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor" Title="Newsletter.razor" HighlightLines="9-10">@Broken</Code>

        <Heading Level="2">Cause</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Browsers post nothing for an unchecked box or an empty multiple select, so the post has no field for the list
            at all. What Blazor does next depends on the rest of the form:
        </TextBlock>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem>
                <strong>Nothing else posts.</strong> Blazor doesn't bind the model, so the property stays <Code>null</Code>, and
                <Code>OnInitialized</Code> sets the defaults again.
            </ListItem>
            <ListItem>
                <strong>Other fields post.</strong> Blazor creates the model and sets the missing list to <Code>null</Code>,
                replacing any list the class starts with.
            </ListItem>
        </List>
        <TextBlock>
            <Code>Checkbox</Code> and <Code>Switch</Code> don't have this problem: a hidden "false" follows each box, so an
            unchecked one still posts. A disabled field posts nothing, like any disabled control.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Fix</Heading>
        <TextBlock>
            Give the defaults only when the request isn't a post, and treat <Code>null</Code> as an empty list wherever you
            read it:
        </TextBlock>
        <Code Block Language="razor" Title="Newsletter.razor" HighlightLines="11-14,16">@Fixed</Code>
        <TextBlock>Uncheck every box and save, in each mode:</TextBlock>
        <ExampleViewer Example="form-empty-selection" ModeSwitch />
        <TextBlock>
            On an interactive page nothing is posted: the list is empty rather than <Code>null</Code>, and the defaults
            apply on the first render. The same code works in every mode.
        </TextBlock>

        <Heading Level="2">Related</Heading>
        <List Gap="2">
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/components/checkbox-group">CheckboxGroup</Anchor> and <Anchor Href="docs/components/multi-select">MultiSelect</Anchor>: what each one posts.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/common/forms">Forms and validation</Anchor>: forms that post on static pages.</ListItem>
            <ListItem><Anchor Href="docs/troubleshooting/form-name">A form's post fails or arrives empty</Anchor>: how a post finds its model.</ListItem>
        </List>
    </ChildContent>
</ArticlePage>

@code {
    private const string Broken = """
        <Form Model="Model" FormName="newsletter" OnValidSubmit="Save">
            <CheckboxGroup @bind-Value="Model!.Topics" Items="Enum.GetValues<Topic>()" />
        </Form>

        @code {
            [SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "newsletter")]
            private Subscription? Model { get; set; }

            protected override void OnInitialized() =>
                Model ??= new() { Topics = [Topic.Releases] };
        }
        """;

    private const string Fixed = """
        <Form Model="Model" FormName="newsletter" OnValidSubmit="Save">
            <CheckboxGroup @bind-Value="Model!.Topics" Items="Enum.GetValues<Topic>()" />
        </Form>

        @code {
            [SupplyParameterFromForm(FormName = "newsletter")]
            private Subscription? Model { get; set; }

            [CascadingParameter] private HttpContext? HttpContext { get; set; }

            protected override void OnInitialized() =>
                Model ??= HttpContext?.Request.Method == "POST"
                    ? new()
                    : new() { Topics = [Topic.Releases] };

            private IReadOnlyList<Topic> Chosen => Model!.Topics ?? [];
        }
        """;
}
